  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "scope": "Both original whole-core bounds retain the SAME signed center under every admissible common coordinate change. Lean proves exact plane-rotation preservation, signed cross energies, and admissibility of finite rational rotation recipes, including recipes starting at identity. For old/new costs C,D, the nonnegative gain max(0,C-D) raises the original floor and lowers its ceiling by the SAME amount; disjoint populations add their actual gains with the same UNEVALUATED E, without a family-count loss. Both the quadratic and further conditioned whole-core costs are covered. All original masks, allocation, factorial orders zero and one, prime counts, unique ownership, full product phase and exterior profile terms remain. The optional enlarged N=10 test retains 32,709,252 labels and all coordinate directions up to cofactor cap 6,484,203. Its quadratic cost falls from about 0.003818 to 0.003406 before sqrt(E), using an explicit rational rotation recipe from identity; the signed center is unchanged. These floating costs are NOT Lean numerical certificates, the population omits earlier nested core deletions, and E is not evaluated. Exact coordinate admissibility is not certification of the cost comparison or of eventual decay. Neither the signed center nor the resulting large-order cost has the sufficient source-scale bound. Both whole -79/1000 floor and 3/2 ceiling remain OPEN; no new zero exclusion or RH claim.",
